<div>
  <img decoding="async" width="696" height="392" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1687687090-768x432-1.jpg" class="attachment-medium_large size-medium_large wp-post-image" alt="Kalashnikov Eyes Digital Ruble Settlements as Russia Aims to Replace ‘Dirty Money’" loading="lazy" style="float:left; margin:0 15px 15px 0;" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1687687090-768x432-1.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1687687090-300x169.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1687687090-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1687687090-696x392.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1687687090-1068x601.jpg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1687687090-747x420.jpg 747w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1687687090-190x107.jpg 190w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1687687090-380x214.jpg 380w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1687687090-760x428.jpg 760w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1687687090.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 696px) 100vw, 696px" /></p> 
  
  <p>
    <strong>Kalashnikov Group, the Russian firearms manufacturer, is ready</strong><strong> to transition to settlements in digital currency. The announcement came from the international economic forum in Saint Petersburg where the central bank of Russia reaffirmed its intention to replace “dirty” and “infectious” paper cash with the digital ruble that’s currently under development. </strong>
  </p>
  
  <h2 style="text-align: center;">
    Russia’s Kalashnikov Concern Looks Forward to Adopting the Digital Ruble
  </h2>
  
  <p>
    The leading Russian gunmaker, Kalashnikov Group, would like to switch to digital currency settlements, owner Alan Lushnikov said during the St. Petersburg International Economic Forum. The event held annually in Russia’s second-largest city gathers government officials and business leaders from well over 100 countries who discuss ways to overcome economic barriers between their nations and the Russian Federation. Quoted by TASS, Lushnikov stated:
  </p>
  
  <blockquote>
    <p>
      What we would expect the banking system to do is to switch to a non-banking system of settlements. Digital currencies are spoken about all the time. This is what we very much need.
    </p>
  </blockquote>
  
  <p>
    A digital currency system would not be linked to SWIFT, the international bank messaging network, and wouldn’t be controlled by bankers, emphasized Alan Lushnikov who has in the past served as deputy minister of transport. Russia, which is under Western sanctions over the annexation of Crimea and Moscow’s involvement in the Ukrainian conflict, has been threatened by the EU and the U.S. with disconnection from the interbank payment system.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="aligncenter wp-image-463998 size-full" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1167709486.jpg" alt="Kalashnikov Eyes Digital Ruble Settlements as Russia Aims to Replace ‘Dirty Money’" width="1280" height="720" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1167709486.jpg 1280w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1167709486-300x169.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1167709486-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1167709486-768x432.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1167709486-696x392.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1167709486-1068x601.jpg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1167709486-747x420.jpg 747w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1167709486-190x107.jpg 190w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1167709486-380x214.jpg 380w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1167709486-760x428.jpg 760w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px" />
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Dozens of central banks around the world are working on projects to issue national digital currencies, including those of China, the United States, and the Eurozone. Bank of Russia is preparing to unveil a prototype of the digital ruble towards the end of 2021. Commenting on the matter, its deputy governor Olga Skorobogatova said in December that the development of central bank digital currencies (CBDCs) can render obsolete traditional banking systems such as SWIFT.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <!-- growjs zone placement 31 -->
    
    <ins> <ins class="growjs-placement"></ins> </ins> <!-- end of growjs zone placement -->
  </p>
  
  <h2 style="text-align: center;">
    Digital Currency to Replace ‘Dirty’ Paper Cash, Central Bank Official Says
  </h2>
  
  <p>
    Cash, as we know it today, is a fading technology, according to Skorobogatova’s colleague, First Deputy Chairman of the Bank of Russia, Sergei Shvetsov. Within a few decades, paper money will be considered marginal and will eventually be replaced by digital currencies, the high-ranking official said at the Saint Petersburg forum. He was quoted by TASS noting that cash is not just “dirty,” but can also spread infections, in the light of the ongoing Covid crisis:
  </p>
  
  <blockquote>
    <p>
      They say “dirty money,” but now it’s also infectious. Certainly, it’s just an obsolete technology.
    </p>
  </blockquote>
  
  <p>
    Shvetsov noted that the coronavirus pandemic has contributed to the abandonment of cash. In his opinion, even now paper banknotes are mostly used either to serve the “gray business,” or in the absence of alternatives allowing non-cash payments.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    “I think that someday, in 20 to 30 years, cash will be marginal. The digital ruble should replace it,” the deputy governor elaborated, stressing that the Bank of Russia is yet to take a final decision on the project’s future. And the speed of its development would depend on the “technological preparedness,” Shvetsov pointed out.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <strong><em>What’s your opinion about central bank digital currencies? Share your thoughts on the subject in the comments section below. </em></strong>
  </p>
